===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|en|enm|no}}, {{m|enm|na}}, from {{inh|en|ang|nā}}, {{m|ang|nō|t=no, not, not ever, never}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*naiwō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*naiwô|t=never}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*ne|t=not}} + {{m|gem-pro|*aiwō|t=ever}}, equivalent to {{com|en|ne|aye}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|na|t=no}}, {{cog|stq|noa|t=no}}, {{cog|fy|né|t=no}}, {{m|fy|nea|t=never}}, {{cog|nl|nee|t=no}}, {{cog|nds|nee|t=no}}, {{cog|de|nie|t=never}}, dialectal {{cog|de|nö|t=no}}, {{cog|da|nej|t=no}}, {{cog|sv|nej|t=no}}, {{cog|is|nei|t=no}}. {{doublet|en|nay}}.

====Adverb====
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|with following adjective}} [[not|Not]], not at all.
## {{n-g|Used before ''[[different]]'', before comparatives with {{m|en|more}} and {{m|en|less}}, and idiomatically before other comparatives.}}
##: {{ux|en|It is a less physical kind of torture, but '''no''' less gruesome.}}
##: {{ux|en|I can think of '''no''' more deserving cause.}}
##: {{ux|en|Look '''no''' further than one's nose.}}
##: {{ux|en|This is '''no''' different from what we've been doing all along.}}
##: {{ux|en|Is your sister any better? ~ '''No''' different. Still ill.}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} {{n-g|Used idiomatically before certain other adjectives.}}
##: {{ux|en|This thing is '''no''' good.}}
##: {{ux|en|The teacher’s decision was '''no''' fair.}}
# {{lb|en|without adjective|now|Scotland|informal}} [[not|Not]].
#: {{ux|en|I just want to find out whether she's coming or '''no'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Can [[ye]] '''no''' help me?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1725|author=w:Daniel Defoe|title=An essay on the history and reality of apparitions
|passage=AS the ''Devil'' is not so Black as he is Painted, so neither does he appear in so many Shapes as we make for him; we Dress him up in more Suits of Cloaths, and more Masquerade Habits, than ever he wore; and I question much, if he was to see the Pictures and Figures which we call ''Devil'', whether he would know himself by some of them or '''no'''.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|usually|humorous}} Not, does not, do not, etc.
#: {{ux|en|[[Ug]] '''no''' like veggie.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When used humorously to mean {{m-g|not}} or {{m-g|does not}}, this word usually implies a simplistic or [[caveman]]-like way of speaking.

