# {{lb|en|intransitive|colloquial}} To [[say]] {{m-g|no}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1983|author=Sasha Moorsom|chapter=5|title=In the Shadow of the Paradise Tree|location=London&#59; Melbourne, Vic.&#59; Henley-on-Thame, Oxfordshire|publisher=[[w:Routledge|Routledge & Kegan Paul]]|page=80|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/inshadowofparadi0000moor/page/80/mode/1up|isbn=0-7100-9408-6|passage=She felt disquiet at these tales of Musa’s illicit activities. ‘Does your father know?’ / ‘My father always '''noes'''. He never yeses. Specially when he’s sick, then he '''noes''' all the time. I gotta get out. Can’t stick around the house with him yelling.{{nb...}}’}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|colloquial}} To [[answer]] with {{m-g|no}}; to [[decline]], [[reject]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1835|month=April|title=The Whimsey Papers.—No. II. Vague Conclusions Concerning Selfishness and Benevolence—Vivid the Casuist—Skinflint the Misanthrope—Green, the Good-Natured Man.|editor={{quote-gloss|{{w|Caroline Norton}}}}|journal=[[w:La Belle Assemblée|The Court Magazine,]]{{nb...|Containing Original Papers, by Distinguished Writers, and Finely Engraved Portraits, Landscapes, and Costumes, from Paintings by Eminent Masters.}}|volume=VI|issue=IV|location=London|publisher=Edward Churton,{{nb...|Holles Street, Cavendish Square. (Late Bull and Churton.)}}|page=168|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/courtmagazinean00critgoog/page/n190/mode/1up|column=1|oclc=265367566|passage=Never accustom yourself to say ‘Yes,’—practise an emphatic and decisive enunciation of the far more dignified and important monosyllable, ‘No.’ {{...}} Believe me, it is of the utmost importance (the advice is not of recent date) that you should '''''No''''' the world.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=17 March 1940|title=Back of the CAA Fight: Independence or Closer Executive Control of Aviation Agency|editor=[[w:David Lawrence (publisher)|David Lawrence]]|journal=[[w:U.S. News & World Report|The United States News]]|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=United States News Publishing Corporation|page=33|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_u-s-news-weekly-special-issues_1940-05-17_8_20/page/33/mode/1up|column=2|issn=2834-4936|oclc=2436843|passage=BUDGET DIRECTOR SMITH / The President yessed his report {{...}} SENATOR McCARRAN / He '''noed''' the President’s report}}

